  "overview": {
    "short": "New Delhi, India’s ceremonial capital, is defined by Sir Edwin Lutyens’ majestic tree-lined boulevards, Kartavya Path, the presidential estate of Rashtrapati Bhavan, and tranquil spiritual sanctuaries.",
    "description": "Conceived in 1911 as the imperial capital of British India and designed by architects Sir Edwin Lutyens and Sir Herbert Baker, New Delhi is renowned for its grand axial vistas, neoclassical sandstone government palaces, and expansive green canopies. From the 42-metre triumphal arch at India Gate and the sprawling ceremonial lawns of Kartavya Path to the peaceful marble petals of Lotus Temple, the sacred healing waters of Gurudwara Bangla Sahib, and the historic tombs within Lodhi Garden, New Delhi represents the majestic civic and cultural heart of modern India.",
